      "title": "Expression of Interest – School of Psychological Sciences Casual Tutors",
      "description": "Expression of Interest – School of Psychological Sciences Casual Tutors - Hobart, TAS, Australia - Launceston, TAS, Australia - Burnie, TAS, Australia Skip to main content Visit UTAS My Profile Kiosk mode Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Expression of Interest – School of Psychological Sciences Casual Tutors 504399 Burnie, TAS Hobart, TAS Launceston, TAS Casual Closing on: 12 Nov 2026 Access flexible casual teaching opportunities that align with your availability and expertise Join a supportive team and help develop the next generation of your profession Available across multiple University locations – Burnie, Hobart and Launceston About the Role As a casual academic you will support teaching within the Bachelor of Psychological Sciences and related postgraduate programs. Typical responsibilities include delivering tutorials and workshops.. Depending on requirements, responsibilities may also include student support, marking, invigilation, and providing assistance in developing teaching materials. How to Register: To express your interest, please submit the following as part of your application: Cover letter (1 page) outlining your motivation for joining this role Resume Copies of relevant qualifications and certifications Any preferred locations and availability Expressions of Interest will be assessed on receipt. You will be contacted if opportunities matching your skills and experience become available. Please note: Your application does not guarantee casual opportunities. Eligibility: Applicants must have: A four-year or equivalent tertiary qualification in a relevant field and/or equivalent qualifications and/or professional experience. A demonstrated understanding of psychological science concepts and methods. Academic, clinical, and/or professional experience relevant to the position. High level communication skills with a demonstrated ability to build rapport with a diverse range of organisations and people, and to work collaboratively and harmoniously as a valued member of a team Desirable: Experience in University-level education within the field of expertise. Tasmanian Working With Vulnerable People Registration Position Description - 504399 - School of Psychological Sciences Casual EOI.pdf Enquiries: For further information about this Expression of Interest, please contact: ppsw.pda@utas.edu.au Recommended Jobs Application Support Analyst Burnie, TAS. Hobart, TAS. Launceston, TAS Information Technology Join a collaborative IT team where you'll play a key role in supporting and enhancing enterprise applications that make a real impact across the University. Unigym Fitness Coordinator Hobart, TAS Administration, Student Services Lead UniGym fitness programs, staff and member services, delivering safe, engaging health and wellbeing experiences at Sandy Bay. Senior Lecturer in Therapeutics and Pharmacy Practice Sydney, NSW Teaching Intensive Make a lasting impact on the future healthcare workforce by leading teaching in therapeutics and pharmacy practice across nursing, pharmacy and other health disciplines within the University of Tasmania’s Health Portfolio © 2026  University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Cookie Preferences Copyright Statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
