    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/jobs/unigym-fitness-coordinator-hobart-tas-australia": {
      "title": "Unigym Fitness Coordinator",
      "description": "Unigym Fitness Coordinator - Hobart, TAS, Australia Skip to main content Visit UTAS My Profile Kiosk mode Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Unigym Fitness Coordinator 504375 Hobart, TAS Full time Closing on: 15 Nov 2026 The University of Tasmania acknowledges the Palawa/Pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. Lead the development and delivery of innovative fitness, wellbeing and group fitness programs at UniGym. Coordinate fitness instructors, personal trainers and contracted fitness services while supporting a safe, welcoming and high-quality member experience. Full-time, ongoing position based in Sandy Bay. About the opportunity As part of the Sport, Campus Life team, the UniGym Fitness Coordinator is responsible for coordinating fitness programs, services and activities that support student, staff and community wellbeing. The role works closely with members, fitness staff and University stakeholders to deliver a high-quality fitness experience while ensuring facilities, equipment and services are safe, welcoming and well maintained. The position supports the ongoing growth and success of UniGym through program development, staff coordination, community engagement and operational oversight. What you'll do Develop and deliver engaging fitness, health and wellbeing programs including group fitness classes and personal training services. Coordinate fitness instructors and personal training staff, including rostering, training records, leave approvals and payroll support. Support planning, budgeting, reporting and operational activities for UniGym programs and services. Build strong relationships with students, staff, members and external stakeholders to enhance participation and member engagement. Ensure fitness facilities, equipment and class spaces are maintained to a high standard of safety and presentation. Support contracted fitness programs and ensure service delivery obligations are met. Generate operational reports and support compliance with relevant health, safety and training requirements. What we're looking for Experience coordinating fitness programs, gym operations or health and wellbeing services. Demonstrated experience delivering group fitness classes and/or personal training services. Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to engage effectively with a diverse range of people. Proven organisational skills and the ability to manage competing priorities in a busy environment. Strong customer service focus and experience using administrative systems and Microsoft Office applications. Knowledge of fitness facility operations, equipment maintenance, safety practices and risk management. Salary details Appointment to this role will be at HEO 6 and will have a total remuneration package of up to $116,872 comprising base salary within $92,120 to $99,891 plus 17% superannuation. How to Apply To apply online, please provide your CV and a 1-2 page cover letter outlining your interest in the role, skills, capabilities and experience. You do not need to separately address the success profile. For further information about this position, please contact Kieran Perry, Head of Sport at Kieran.Perry@utas.edu.au Please visit https://www.utas.edu.au/jobs/applying for our guide to applying and details on the recruitment process. For current UTAS staff, in submitting your application, you acknowledge you have/intend to discuss your interest in this vacancy with your current manager and understand they may need to be contacted confidentially by the hiring manager as part of the assessment of your application. Please refer to the attached Position Description for full details. Position Description - UniGym Fitness Coordinator.pdf Applications close: Sunday, 15th November 2026, 11:55pm As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of this role. Recommended Jobs Senior Lecturer in Therapeutics and Pharmacy Practice Sydney, NSW Teaching Intensive Make a lasting impact on the future healthcare workforce by leading teaching in therapeutics and pharmacy practice across nursing, pharmacy and other health disciplines within the University of Tasmania’s Health Portfolio Operations Support Officer, Health Partnerships Sydney, NSW Administration Health Partnerships are seeking to appoint an Operations Support Officer in this ongoing role! AFWI Research Contracts Manager Hobart, TAS. Launceston, TAS. Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS Laboratory & Research Support, Legal & Compliance, Management Support nationally significant research by leading contract management and governance across AFWI's research portfolio. © 2026  University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Cookie Preferences Copyright Statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
