    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/jobs/senior-lecturer-in-therapeutics-and-pharmacy-practice-sydney-nsw-australia": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer in Therapeutics and Pharmacy Practice",
      "description": "Senior Lecturer in Therapeutics and Pharmacy Practice - Sydney, NSW, Australia Skip to main content Visit UTAS My Profile Kiosk mode Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 0:00 Loaded : 0% Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 0:00 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles captions and subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Senior Lecturer in Therapeutics and Pharmacy Practice 504389 Sydney, NSW Full time Closing on: 15 Nov 2026 The University of Tasmania acknowledges the Palawa/Pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. Lead teaching in therapeutics and pharmacy practice for nursing and other health students in Sydney, while supporting the delivery of our pharmacy programs remotely Join a collaborative academic community with opportunities to contribute to educational innovation, research and professional engagement Full-time, ongoing role based at our Rozelle Campus, Sydney, commencing January 2027 About the opportunity Based at our Sydney (Rozelle) campus, this is an opportunity for an experienced pharmacy educator or practitioner to bring their expertise to a teaching-focused senior academic role within the University of Tasmania's School of Pharmacy and Pharmacology. This position plays a critical role in leading therapeutics and pharmacy practice teaching for nursing and other health students in Sydney, bringing medicines expertise into interprofessional health education. The role will also support teaching across our pharmacy programs through digitally enabled delivery within the University's multi-campus learning environment. Working across a connected, multi-campus learning environment, you will provide leadership in learning and teaching, coordinate key areas of the curriculum, deliver and support teaching across locations using contemporary digital approaches, mentor colleagues, and contribute to the ongoing development of innovative and engaging learning experiences. This role is ideally suited to a registered pharmacist with significant clinical expertise and a passion for education. You will bring either a PhD or an equivalent combination of professional standing, academic achievement and clinical experience, along with the ability to foster teaching excellence and support the development of colleagues. While the position is based in Sydney, occasional travel to Tasmania may be required as part of our connected, multi-campus approach to learning and collaboration. What you’ll do: Lead and deliver high-quality learning and teaching in therapeutics and pharmacy practice across nursing, pharmacy and other health programs, with a particular focus on interprofessional medicines education. Support teaching and curriculum delivery across the School's pharmacy programs through remote, digitally enabled and multi-campus teaching. Drive curriculum innovation and teaching excellence, developing contemporary learning experiences that improve educational practice across courses, cohorts and campuses. Provide academic leadership and mentorship, supporting colleagues, sharing expertise, and contributing to a culture of continuous improvement. Contribute to research and scholarship in pharmacy, building the evidence base for practice through research, publications, and collaboration. Build and strengthen partnerships with the pharmacy profession, healthcare sector, industry, and broader community to enhance teaching, research and workforce outcomes. ­ What we’re looking for: Contemporary clinical expertise in therapeutics and pharmacy practice, with advanced scope of practice qualifications highly regarded. Demonstrated excellence in university-level teaching and learning, including curriculum development and unit coordination, with the ability to deliver high-quality teaching across face-to-face, online and multi-campus environments. Demonstrated ability to contribute to interprofessional learning and to teach therapeutics and medicines-related content across pharmacy, nursing and other health disciplines. Ability to provide academic leadership, mentor colleagues, and contribute to teaching innovation and student success. A strong track record of building effective partnerships with the pharmacy profession, healthcare organisations, industry and the wider community. Proven ability to work collaboratively within multidisciplinary teams and contribute positively to a shared culture and goals. An emerging or established research profile, evidenced through publications, conference presentations, research supervision and/or success in attracting funding. Salary details Appointment to this role will be at Academic Level C and will have a total remuneration package of up to $184,076 comprising base salary within the range of $138,536 to $157,330 plus 17% superannuation. How to Apply Applications for this role should include your CV and a cover letter that addresses the ‘Role Specific Skills, Knowledge and Experience’ for this position. For further information about this position, please contact Lisa Cavanagh, Executive Assistant to Head of School, Lisa.Cavanagh@utas.edu.au Please visit https://www.utas.edu.au/jobs/applying for our guide to applying and details on the recruitment process. For current UTAS staff, in submitting your application, you acknowledge you have/intend to discuss your interest in this vacancy with your current manager and understand they may need to be contacted confidentially by the hiring manager as part of the assessment of your application. Please refer to the attached Position Description Below for full details. Position Description - Senior Lecturer in Therapeutics Pharmacy Practice (504389).pdf Applications close Sunday, 15 November 2026, 11.55pm As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of this role. Back to job search Recommended Jobs Unigym Fitness Coordinator Hobart, TAS Administration, Student Services Lead UniGym fitness programs, staff and member services, delivering safe, engaging health and wellbeing experiences at Sandy Bay. Operations Support Officer, Health Partnerships Sydney, NSW Administration Health Partnerships are seeking to appoint an Operations Support Officer in this ongoing role! AFWI Research Contracts Manager Hobart, TAS. Launceston, TAS. Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS Laboratory & Research Support, Legal & Compliance, Management Support nationally significant research by leading contract management and governance across AFWI's research portfolio. © 2026  University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Cookie Preferences Copyright Statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
