      "description": "Operations Support Officer, Health Partnerships - Sydney, NSW, Australia Skip to main content Visit UTAS My Profile Kiosk mode Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 0:00 Loaded : 0% Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 0:00 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles captions and subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Operations Support Officer, Health Partnerships 504454 Sydney, NSW Part time Closing on: 12 Nov 2026 Prepare high-quality briefing notes, background papers and talking points to support stakeholder engagements Provide outstanding operational and project support in this pivotal role Part time (0.8), ongoing role based at our Rozelle campus! About the opportunity The Operations Support Officer, Health Partnerships provides high-quality operational, project and administrative support to the Director Health Partnerships and the broader Health Partnerships team, supporting the delivery of strategic partnerships, clinical placements, compliance activities, quality improvement initiatives and operational priorities across UTAS Health. The position is also responsible for maintaining partnership and placement records, communication channels, project dashboards, and collaboration platforms, while identifying opportunities to improve processes, and support efficient, consistent and effective business operations across the Health Partnerships portfolio. What you’ll do: Provide comprehensive operational, project and administrative support. Manage and quality assure communications, correspondence, reports, briefing materials and meeting documentation. Support the coordination of projects, initiatives and operational activities across the portfolio. Ensure the Director Health Partnerships is well prepared for meetings and engagements through proactive support. Engage proactively with Health staff and external partners to facilitate responsive and professional coordinated support.­ What we’re looking for: Experience in providing high-level operational, project or administrative support in a complex organisation. Highly developed written, verbal and interpersonal communication skills. Experience coordinating multiple projects and operational activities. Proven ability to build and maintain effective relationships with senior leaders, academic staff, professional staff and external stakeholders. Demonstrated ability to identify inefficiencies, establish, maintain and improve systems, processes and records. Salary details Appointment to this role will be at HEO 5 and will have a total remuneration package of up to $105,665 comprising base salary within the range of $80,869 to $90,312 plus 17% superannuation. How to Apply To apply online, please provide your CV and 1-2-page cover letter outlining your interest in the role, skills, capabilities and experience.  You do not need to separately address the success profile. For further information about this position, please contact Michelle Phillips, Director Health Partnerships, Michelle.Phillips@utas.edu.au Please visit https://www.utas.edu.au/jobs/applying for our guide to applying and details on the recruitment process. For current UTAS staff, in submitting your application, you acknowledge you have/intend to discuss your interest in this vacancy with your current manager and understand they may need to be contacted confidentially by the hiring manager as part of the assessment of your application. Please refer to the attached Position Description Below for full details. Position Description - 504454 - Operations Support Officer, Health Partnerships.pdf Applications close Thursday, 12 November 2026, 11.55pm As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of this role. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 0f4355a1 Last Name (required) ed6bb68a Email (required) 7c75f3c6 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Unigym Fitness Coordinator Hobart, TAS Administration, Student Services Lead UniGym fitness programs, staff and member services, delivering safe, engaging health and wellbeing experiences at Sandy Bay. Senior Lecturer in Therapeutics and Pharmacy Practice Sydney, NSW Teaching Intensive Make a lasting impact on the future healthcare workforce by leading teaching in therapeutics and pharmacy practice across nursing, pharmacy and other health disciplines within the University of Tasmania’s Health Portfolio AFWI Research Contracts Manager Hobart, TAS. Launceston, TAS. Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS Laboratory & Research Support, Legal & Compliance, Management Support nationally significant research by leading contract management and governance across AF