    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/jobs/senior-lecturer-psychology-statewide-all-locations-in-tasmania-tas-australia-hobart": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer Psychology",
      "description": "Senior Lecturer Psychology - Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS, Australia - Hobart, TAS, Australia Skip to main content Visit UTAS My Profile Kiosk mode Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Senior Lecturer Psychology 504456 Hobart, TAS Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS Full time Closing on: 15 Nov 2026 The University of Tasmania acknowledges the palawa/pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. Provide academic leadership in psychology education and professional training. Teach and supervise students across undergraduate and postgraduate programs. Contribute to impactful research and strengthen psychology workforce outcomes for Tasmania and beyond. Full time, Academic Level C opportunity based in Tasmania. About the Opportunity The University of Tasmania is seeking an experienced and collaborative psychologist to join the School of Psychological Sciences as a Senior Lecturer. Working within a student-centred academic environment, you will play an important role in preparing future psychologists through outstanding teaching, placement supervision, curriculum development and professional practice education. You will work closely with academic colleagues, professional staff and industry partners to ensure our programs continue to meet contemporary professional and accreditation standards while responding to workforce and mental health needs across Tasmania and beyond. This role offers an opportunity to contribute to a university committed to making a difference for Tasmania while helping shape the future of psychology education, clinical training and research. What you’ll do Make an effective and sustained contribution to the University's strategic objectives and academic mission. Deliver high-quality teaching across undergraduate and postgraduate psychology programs. Provide supervision and support for students undertaking professional practice placements. Contribute to curriculum development and continuous improvement aligned with accreditation requirements. Undertake high-quality research and scholarly activity. Supervise higher degree research students. Build and maintain productive partnerships with the psychology profession, health services and community stakeholders. Contribute to a collaborative and inclusive academic culture. What we’re looking for A PhD or equivalent in Psychology. Current registration as a psychologist with AHPRA with no reprimands, undertakings or conditions. Hold a current Working with Vulnerable People (WWVP). Psychology Board of Australia Approved Supervisor status. Demonstrated success in university-level teaching and learning. Knowledge of Australian Psychology Accreditation Council (APAC) accreditation standards and their application in curriculum design. A strong research track record, including publications and scholarly contributions. Experience supervising provisionally registered psychologists. Clinical experience relevant to the position. A demonstrated ability to build effective relationships across the profession, industry and community. What’s on Offer? As we look toward 2050, we remain committed to fostering excellence, collaboration, and transformative education - preparing graduates to navigate the challenges of a rapidly changing world and shape its future. While remaining true to our Tasmanian roots, this career defining role will see you significantly contribute to our dedication to making a difference for, and from, Tasmania. You’ll have access an array of staff benefits and discounts including. 26 Weeks paid parental leave for primary care givers 17% Superannuation contribution Health and fitness membership options Accommodation and Car Hire discounts Health Insurance and Banking Novated Leasing Salary details Appointment to this role will be at Academic Level C and will have a total remuneration package of up to $184,076 comprising base salary within the range of $138,536 to $157,330 plus 17% superannuation. How to Apply? To apply online, please provide the following supporting documentation: Resume Cover letter outlining your suitability and motivation for the role Your responses to the success criteria from the Position Description below For further information about this position, please contact Kimberley Norris, Head of School, School of Psychological Sciences Kimberley.Norris@utas.edu.au Please visit https://www.utas.edu.au/jobs/applying for our guide to applying and details on the recruitment process. For current UTAS staff, in submitting your application, you acknowledge you have/intend to discuss your interest in this vacancy with your current manager and understand they may need to be contacted confidentially by the hiring manager as part of the assessment of your application. Please refer to the attached Position Description Below for full details. Position Description - Senior Lecturer Psychology.pdf Applications close Sunday 15 November 2026, 11.55pm As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of this role. Recommended Jobs AFWI Research Contracts Manager Hobart, TAS. Launceston, TAS. Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS Laboratory & Research Support, Legal & Compliance, Management Support nationally significant research by leading contract management and governance across AFWI's research portfolio. Technical Officer Launceston, TAS Infrastructure & Property, Teaching Support Firefighter, defence, maintenance or trade background? Put your practical skills to work at the Australian Maritime College's Emergency Response Centre and help train the next generation of maritime professionals Cultural Collections Officer (Tyler Collection) Hobart, TAS Library Support the ethical care, display and activation of collections, bringing the Tyler Collection of Romanian and Modern Art to life for teaching, research and public engagement. © 2026  University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Cookie Preferences Copyright Statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
    },
    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/jobs/lecturer-senior-lecturer-in-health-sociology-indigenous-statewide-all-locations-in-tasmania-tas-australia-hobart-launceston": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Health Sociology (Indigenous)",
      "description": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Health Sociology (Indigenous) - Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS, Australia - Hobart, TAS, Australia - Launceston, TAS, Australia Skip to main content Visit UTAS My Profile Kiosk mode Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:26 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:26 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Health Sociology (Indigenous) 504311 Hobart, TAS Launceston, TAS Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS Full time Closing on: 28 Oct 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Teach Health Sociology across undergraduate and postgraduate programs Shape health research and education through Aboriginal knowledges and partnerships Full time, ongoing position based in Launceston or Hobart The University of Tasmania acknowledges the Palawa/Pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We pay our respects to Elders past and present who hold memories, knowledges and culture, and their enduring cultural practices of caring for Country that spans millennia. About the Opportunity As the Lecturer or Senior Lecturer in Health Sociology, you will deliver high-quality teaching across undergraduate and postgraduate programs, with a particular focus on embedding Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander knowledges and perspectives. Working collaboratively, you will contribute to teaching, research and partnerships that strengthen culturally responsive approaches to health and address health inequalities and inequities. In addition, you will: Embed Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander knowledges and perspectives across Sociology and Humanities and Social Sciences teaching. Contribute to teaching and curriculum development within nursing and allied health programs. Undertake high-quality research that contributes to the school’s research excellence and impact. Supervise research higher degree students and support their successful completion. Provide academic leadership and contribute to outstanding learning and teaching. Build productive relationships with Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander stakeholders, students, colleagues and community. Contribute to collaborative research, teaching and engagement across the University and with external partners. About the University At the University of Tasmania, we have a mission to make a difference for Tasmania, and from Tasmania. With our unique location and history, we have both an obligation and opportunity to make a global contribution. People are at the heart of that contribution. We focus on building a workplace culture where we come together in a way that empowers us all to connect, belong and grow. The University is one of the largest employers in our State, with campuses in three distinct regions: Hobart, Launceston, and Burnie. We also have a specialised health campus in Sydney. We strive to stimulate economic growth, lift literacy, improve health outcomes for Tasmania and nurture our environment as it nurtures us. We welcome enquiring minds, from near and far, to join us in our pursuit of the extraordinary. What’s Required For Level B (Lecturer) A PhD or equivalent qualification in a relevant social science field. A demonstrated record of, and a continuing commitment to research in the field of health sociology. University-level teaching experience across online and face-to-face delivery. Experience building and maintaining productive relationships with the discipline, health professions, Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander people and/or wider community. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to engage thoughtfully with students and staff from diverse backgrounds and cultures. The ability to work effectively both independently and collaboratively within discipline-based and multidisciplinary teams. For Level C (Senior Lecturer) (in addition to the above) A strong record in, and continuing commitment to, research that has made notable contributions to the field of health sociology. A record of research higher degree supervision and completions, relative to opportunity. Demonstrated achievement in University-level teaching and learning across different delivery modes. A record of contributing effectively to building and maintaining effective and productive links locally and nationally with the discipline, health professions, Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander people, and/or wider community. This is an Identified Position. You must be an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person to be considered for this opportunity. Candidates must provide eligibility documentation with their application. Please contact aboriginal.employment@utas.edu.au to discuss the documentation required. What’s on Offer? On offer is a full time, ongoing opportunity based in Launceston or Hobart with a competitive remuneration package. We value our staff and the important contributions they make to our community. You’ll have access to an array of staff benefits and discounts including: 26 weeks paid parental leave for primary care givers 5 days Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Cultural leave annually 17% superannuation contribution Health and fitness membership options Accommodation and car hire discounts Health insurance and banking Novated Leasing Relocation support available for those considering a move to Tasmania Belong - Be You People are at the heart of everything we do. Our vision is to ensure that our people feel encouraged and supported to bring their whole selves to work. Fostering diversity and inclusion is our key priority, supporting our communities to come together in ways that empower connection, learning, belonging and growth. Celebrating the strengths that diversity brings will enable us to achieve our vision and mission. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community. Tell us how we can make this job work for you. Remuneration Appointment to this role will be at Academic Level B or C and will have a remuneration package of up to $184,076, comprising of a base salary within the range of $114,766 to $157,330 plus 17% superannuation. How to Apply? If this role is of interest, we look forward to hearing from you. Please provide your up-to-date resume A 1–2-page cover letter outlining your motivation for the role And a statement addressing the selection criteria by outlining how your skills and experience align with the role specific skills, knowledge and experience in the Position Description For further information about this position, please contact Professor Vaughan Higgins, Professor, Sociology at vaughan.higgins@utas.edu.au , Associate Professor Peta Cook, Associate Professor in Sociology at peta.cook@utas.edu.au or aboriginal.employment@utas.edu.au . Applications close 11:55pm Wednesday 28th of October 2026 Lecturer-Senior Lecturer in Health Sociology (Indigenous) Position Description.pdf Looking for another Health Sociology opportunity? We are also recruiting for a Lecturer in Health Sociology. Take a look at our other role and explore which opportunity is the right fit for you. As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of this role. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) bca0d043 Last Name (required) 1a9146da Email (required) 5141834d Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Learning Adviser (STEM/Numeracy) Hobart, TAS Student Services, Teaching Support Deliver specialist learning development support in STEM-related areas, including numeracy, mathematics, statistics, quantitative reasoning, scientific literacy and data interpretation. Lecturer in English Hobart, TAS. Launceston, TAS Teaching Intensive Shape the future of English education and inspire the next generation of readers, writers and critical thinkers through innovative and engaging learning experiences Teaching Laboratory Technician Hobart, TAS Laboratory & Research Support Play a key role in supporting hands-on teaching and learning, helping to deliver safe, engaging and well-organised laboratory experiences for our students Sign up for job alerts Job Alert d2d60c64 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Teaching Intensive Teaching Intensive Employment Type Full time Full time Locations Hobart, TAS, Australia 