    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/jobs/lecturer-in-medical-sciences-launceston-tas-australia": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Medical Sciences",
      "description": "Lecturer in Medical Sciences - Launceston, TAS, Australia Skip to main content Visit UTAS My Profile Kiosk mode Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:26 Loaded : 0% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:26 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Lecturer in Medical Sciences 504427 Launceston, TAS Part time Closing on: 19 Nov 2026 The University of Tasmania acknowledges the Palawa/Pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. Shape Tasmania's future medical workforce through inspiring medical sciences education Opportunity to combine your disciplinary expertise with meaningful teaching and student mentorship Part-time (0.5 FTE), ongoing position based in Launceston with excellent staff benefits and 17% superannuation About the opportunity We are seeking to appoint a Lecturer in Medical Sciences within the Tasmanian School of Medicine. This position will focus on the delivery of high-quality medical education, including teaching foundational medical sciences across a variety of disciplines and using online and on-campus learning modalities.  This position will support the supply of a skilled medical workforce to Tasmania and is part of the expansion of the Medicine Program which commenced in 2026. The appointee will report to the Launceston Clinical School Director and the Lead Academic for the Medical Sciences program within UTAS and will work with a team of academic staff to deliver medical education in Launceston, Tasmania with a focus on alignment with the Tasmanian School of Medicine and the University of Tasmania’s goals of making significant socially accountable contributions to the health and wellbeing of the Tasmanian community. We welcome applications from experienced health professionals and clinicians interested in transitioning into or expanding their involvement in medical education. What you’ll do: Make an effective and sustained contribution to the University in achieving its strategic objectives and fulfilling its operational responsibilities. Undertake high-quality and scholarly undergraduate teaching across the medical sciences disciplines that underpin the study of medicine, including areas such as anatomy, physiology, bacteriology, pathology and biochemistry. Mentor and support medical students both individually and within small-group learning environments. Contribute to the development and maintenance of productive and effective links inside the University and locally and nationally with the discipline and interdisciplinary colleagues. Seek out and engage in opportunities to continuously improve academic learning and teaching skills. What we’re looking for: Tertiary qualifications in a relevant medical sciences discipline. Experience in undergraduate University-level teaching and learning. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Demonstrated capacity to work effectively with staff, students and external organisations. High-level organisational skills including experience adhering to safe operating procedures. Demonstrated initiative coupled with the ability to work both independently and as a member of a team Salary details Appointment to this role will be at Academic Level B and will have a total remuneration package of up to $155,885 pro-rata comprising base salary within the range of $114,766 pro-rata to $133,235 pro-rata plus 17% superannuation. How to Apply To apply online, please provide your CV and 1-2-page cover letter outlining your interest in the role, skills, capabilities and experience.  You do not need to separately address the Roles Specific Skills, Knowledge and Experience. For further information about this position, please contact Dr Rohan Church, Director Launceston Clinical School, Rohan.Church@utas.edu.au Please visit https://www.utas.edu.au/jobs/applying for our guide to applying and details on the recruitment process. For current UTAS staff, in submitting your application, you acknowledge you have/intend to discuss your interest in this vacancy with your current manager and understand they may need to be contacted confidentially by the hiring manager as part of the assessment of your application. Please refer to the attached Position Description Below for full details. Position Description - Lecturer in Medical Sciences- 504427.pdf Applications close Thursday, 19 November 2026, 11.55pm Shortlisted candidates will be invited to interviews on Wednesday, 25 November 2026 As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of this role. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) b97dff9f Last Name (required) 874cff63 Email (required) b2e2dcc2 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Geophysical Data Engineer Hobart, TAS Information Technology, Laboratory & Research Support Develop data systems, workflows and visualisation tools supporting Antarctic Ice Sheet research, analysis and management of complex datasets. Project Lead Hobart, TAS Community & Engagement, Project Management & Support Lead and coordinate a community-led pilot project in New Norfolk, working with children, families, schools and stakeholders to develop and strengthen educational pathways. Senior Lecturer in Medical Education Launceston, TAS Teaching Intensive Curious about academic medicine? Explore a flexible fixed-term teaching opportunity while maintaining your clinical career Sign up for job alerts Job Alert f7b242aa Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Teaching Intensive Teaching Intensive Employment Type Part time Part time Locations Launceston, TAS, Australia Launceston, TAS, Australia First Name (required) 1882989d Last Name (required) 0aaa33ee Email (required) 433f7d57 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026  University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Cookie Preferences Copyright Statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
