    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/jobs/lecturer-or-senior-lecturer-in-medical-education-launceston-tas-australia": {
      "title": "Lecturer or Senior Lecturer in Medical Education",
      "description": "Lecturer or Senior Lecturer in Medical Education - Launceston, TAS, Australia Skip to main content Visit UTAS My Profile Kiosk mode Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:26 Loaded : 0% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:26 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Lecturer or Senior Lecturer in Medical Education 504424 Launceston, TAS Part time Closing on: 19 Nov 2026 The University of Tasmania acknowledges the Palawa/Pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. Opportunity to shape our future doctors Maintain clinical practice while contributing to academic medicine Part time (0.2 FTE), positions based in Launceston with excellent staff benefits and 17% superannuation About the opportunity The Tasmanian School of Medicine is seeking to appoint Lecturers and/or Senior Lecturers in Medical Education to support the delivery of the Tasmanian Medicine Program (BMedScMD). Based in Launceston, these roles provide an exciting opportunity for clinicians and medical educators to help shape the next generation of doctors while contributing to a contemporary, integrated medical curriculum. Working collaboratively with academic and clinical colleagues, you will deliver high-quality teaching, assessment and student support, while contributing to curriculum development, scholarly activity and the broader educational mission of the School. Through this work, you will support the University of Tasmania's commitment to socially accountable medical education and improving the health and wellbeing of Tasmanian communities. Reporting to the Launceston Clinical School Director, you will join a dedicated team focused on preparing future doctors through innovative, student-centred learning experiences. Appointment may be made at Lecturer (Level B) or Senior Lecturer (Level C) level, depending on qualifications, experience and demonstrated contributions to medical education. These part-time opportunities are an excellent opportunity for clinicians seeking to combine their clinical practice with teaching, mentoring and educational leadership. What you’ll do: Deliver high-quality teaching, assessment and student support within the Tasmanian Medicine Program. Contribute to the design, development and continuous improvement of curriculum and learning experiences. Work collaboratively with academic and clinical colleagues to provide an outstanding student experience. Participate in scholarly activities that enhance teaching quality and medical education practice. Build and maintain relationships with healthcare services, clinicians and community stakeholders. For appointment at Senior Lecturer level, provide leadership in curriculum development, educational innovation and academic mentoring. What we’re looking for: Lecturer (Level B) Demonstrated experience in teaching and assessment in medicine, health sciences or a related discipline. Capacity to contribute to curriculum development and scholarly activity. Ability to work collaboratively with academic and clinical colleagues to deliver high-quality student learning experiences. Senior Lecturer (Level C) Significant experience and demonstrated impact in medical or health professional education. Proven ability to lead curriculum development, educational innovation and quality improvement initiatives. An established record of educational scholarship and/or academic achievement. Demonstrated academic leadership, including mentoring colleagues and contributing to strategic priorities. Qualifications and Licences Working with Vulnerable People check Salary details Appointment to this role will be at Academic Level B or Level C, with a pro-rata salary within the range of $114,766 to $157,330 plus 17% superannuation, depending on skills, experience and qualifications. How to Apply To apply online, please provide your CV and 1-2-page cover letter outlining your interest in the role, skills, capabilities and experience.  You do not need to separately address the Roles Specific Skills, Knowledge and Experience. For further information about this position, please contact Dr Rohan Church, Director Launceston Clinical School, Rohan.Church@utas.edu.au Please visit https://www.utas.edu.au/jobs/applying for our guide to applying and details on the recruitment process. Please refer to the attached Position Description Below for full details. Position Description - Lecturer in Medical Education - (Level B) 2026.pdf Position Description - Senior Lecturer in Medical Education - (Level C) 2026.pdf Applications close Thursday, 19 November 2026, 11.55pm Shortlisted candidates will be invited to interviews on Wednesday, 25 November 2026 As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of this role. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 13346f35 Last Name (required) c9394dae Email (required) 4f032cf1 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Geophysical Data Engineer Hobart, TAS Information Technology, Laboratory & Research Support Develop data systems, workflows and visualisation tools supporting Antarctic Ice Sheet research, analysis and management of complex datasets. Project Lead Hobart, TAS Community & Engagement, Project Management & Support Lead and coordinate a community-led pilot project in New Norfolk, working with children, families, schools and stakeholders to develop and strengthen educational pathways. Senior Lecturer in Medical Education Launceston, TAS Teaching Intensive Curious about academic medicine? Explore a flexible fixed-term teaching opportunity while maintaining your clinical career Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 3844eefa Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Teaching Intensive Teaching Intensive Employment Type Part time Part time Locations Launceston, TAS, Australia Launceston, TAS, Australia First Name (required) 85b7ad04 Last Name (required) 083acf06 Email (required) a4cece0c Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026  University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Cookie Preferences Copyright Statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
