    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/jobs/schools-engagement-facilitator-burnie-tas-australia": {
      "title": "Schools Engagement Facilitator",
      "description": "Schools Engagement Facilitator - Burnie, TAS, Australia Skip to main content Visit UTAS My Profile Kiosk mode Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:26 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:26 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Schools Engagement Facilitator 504420 Burnie, TAS Full time Closing on: 19 Nov 2026 Add to favourites View favourites The University of Tasmania acknowledges the Palawa/Pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. Inspire and engage the next generation of University of Tasmania students Deliver maximum engagement impact in this crucial role Full time, ongoing role based at the stunning Cradle Coast Campus About the opportunity As a Schools Engagement Facilitator, you will be responsible for planning and coordinating school group visits to University campuses. This includes developing activity programs in collaboration with academics and professional staff, overseeing all event logistics, and maintaining clear and timely communication with schools. What you’ll do: Work collaboratively in the Recruitment and Engagement team to design, plan, promote and coordinate the effective delivery of on and off campus school engagement activities. Identify opportunities to increase awareness of course offerings and learning opportunities through engaging with schools and throughout our communities to enhance aspiration for higher education. Support tours and visits to campus for prospective students and school groups ensuring a positive and informative experience. Project manage approved initiatives to ensure that maximum benefits are achieved for all parties. Work with colleagues in the Recruitment and Engagement team to continuously improve and refine processes.­ What we’re looking for: Demonstrated ability to build and maintain successful relationships with key stakeholders. Demonstrated capacity to manage multiple projects and deliver outcomes on time and within budget. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively across a geographically dispersed team. Strong communication and interpersonal skills and the ability to confidently liaise with people of various skills, experience and background to achieve positive outcomes. An understanding of the challenges facing the Tasmanian education sector and the need to increase access and participation across the educational spectrum. Salary details Appointment to this role will be at HEO 6 and will have a total remuneration package of up to $116,872 comprising base salary within the range of $92,120 to $99,891 plus 17% superannuation. How to Apply To apply online, please provide your CV and 1-2-page cover letter outlining your interest in the role, skills, capabilities and experience.  You do not need to separately address the success profile. For further information about this position, please contact Prue Handbury, Manager Educational Outreach, prudence.handbury@utas.edu.au Please visit https://www.utas.edu.au/jobs/applying for our guide to applying and details on the recruitment process. For current UTAS staff, in submitting your application, you acknowledge you have/intend to discuss your interest in this vacancy with your current manager and understand they may need to be contacted confidentially by the hiring manager as part of the assessment of your application. Please refer to the attached Position Description Below for full details. Position Description - 504420 - Schools Engagement Facilitator.pdf Applications close Thursday, 19 November 2026, 11.55pm As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of this role. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) ea9323e6 Last Name (required) a7a1be5a Email (required) a8bdb712 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Geophysical Data Engineer Hobart, TAS Information Technology, Laboratory & Research Support Develop data systems, workflows and visualisation tools supporting Antarctic Ice Sheet research, analysis and management of complex datasets. Project Lead Hobart, TAS Community & Engagement, Project Management & Support Lead and coordinate a community-led pilot project in New Norfolk, working with children, families, schools and stakeholders to develop and strengthen educational pathways. Senior Lecturer in Medical Education Launceston, TAS Teaching Intensive Curious about academic medicine? Explore a flexible fixed-term teaching opportunity while maintaining your clinical career Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 7e00c099 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Community & Engagement Student Services Community & Engagement Student Services Employment Type Full time Full time Locations Burnie, TAS, Australia Burnie, TAS, Australia First Name (required) be9b69aa Last Name (required) 3ad8e55f Email (required) d71951b0 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026  University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Cookie Preferences Copyright Statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
