    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/jobs/technical-officer-launceston-tas-australia-5cc6dc71-d7fd-48fc-9674-11ca5605e8a7": {
      "title": "Technical Officer",
      "description": "Technical Officer - Launceston, TAS, Australia Skip to main content Visit UTAS My Profile Kiosk mode Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:26 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:26 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Technical Officer 504359 Launceston, TAS Full time Closing on: 12 Nov 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Precision Manufacturing and Technical Support Be part of a team delivering innovative maritime and defence research Full time, Fixed Term (2 years) based in Launceston The University of Tasmania acknowledges the Palawa/Pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. About the opportunity The University of Tasmania is seeking a Technical Officer to join the Cavitation Research Laboratory (CRL) at the Australian Maritime College's Newnham Campus. This position plays a key role in supporting the laboratory's research and teaching activities through the manufacture, assembly, maintenance, and operation of specialised equipment and instrumentation. As our new Technical Officer, you will undertake a diverse range of technical activities, including precision machining and subtractive manufacturing, assembly of complex research equipment, plant and facility maintenance, and the application of best practice Work Health and Safety (WHS) standards. Working closely with the CRL team, you will contribute to the successful delivery of innovative research projects and learning outcomes. Funded by the Defence Science and Technology Group (DSTG) Platforms Division, this position provides critical technical expertise to support the development, operation, and continuous improvement of advanced experimental facilities and equipment, enabling the laboratory to achieve its research objectives. What you’ll do: Undertake the machining, fabrication, and assembly of engineering laboratory equipment and instrumentation, ensuring precise fits and adherence to required tolerances. Assist in the development of new equipment and associated accessories. Perform routine maintenance of facilities, equipment, and associated infrastructure to support operational requirements. Apply and promote best practice Work Health and Safety (WHS) principles, policies, and procedures. ­ What we’re looking for: Trade qualification and relevant industry experience in a related technical field. Demonstrated knowledge of computer numerical control (CNC) machining, including subtractive programming, simulation, operation, and other advanced manufacturing methods. Ability to work independently under broad direction while supporting research projects and activities. Ability to assemble and maintain complex, high-precision equipment to a high standard. Demonstrated experience in diagnostics, fault finding, troubleshooting, and problem-solving. Strong ability to work collaboratively with, and follow direction from, academic and professional staff. Salary details Appointment to this role will be at HEO 5 and will have a total remuneration package of up to $105,665 comprising base salary within the range of $80,869 to $90,312 plus 17% superannuation. How to Apply To apply online, please provide your CV and 1-2-page cover letter outlining your interest in the role, skills, capabilities and experience.  You do not need to separately address the success profile. For further information about this position, please contact Robert Wrigley, Senior Technical Officer Team Leader on R.Wrigley@utas.edu.au or 03 63249587. Please visit https://www.utas.edu.au/jobs/applying for our guide to applying and details on the recruitment process. For current UTAS staff, in submitting your application, you acknowledge you have/intend to discuss your interest in this vacancy with your current manager and understand they may need to be contacted confidentially by the hiring manager as part of the assessment of your application. Please refer to the attached Position Description Below for full details. Position Description - 504359 - Technical Officer.pdf Applications close Thursday, 12 November 2026, 11.55pm As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian citizenship and able to obtain and maintain a personal security clearance of Negative Vetting Level 1 (NV1) Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) fa36df71 Last Name (required) 431966ef Email (required) b19ec5b4 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Geophysical Data Engineer Hobart, TAS Information Technology, Laboratory & Research Support Develop data systems, workflows and visualisation tools supporting Antarctic Ice Sheet research, analysis and management of complex datasets. Project Lead Hobart, TAS Community & Engagement, Project Management & Support Lead and coordinate a community-led pilot project in New Norfolk, working with children, families, schools and stakeholders to develop and strengthen educational pathways. Senior Lecturer in Medical Education Launceston, TAS Teaching Intensive Curious about academic medicine? Explore a flexible fixed-term teaching opportunity while maintaining your clinical career Sign up for job alerts Job Alert e13169b8 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Laboratory & Research Support Teaching Support Laboratory & Research Support Teaching Support Employment Type Full time Full time Locations Launceston, TAS, Australia Launceston, TAS, Australia First Name (required) 50341a50 Last Name (required) b8386756 Email (required) 2fb5a2fb Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026  University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Cookie Preferences Copyright Statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
