    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/jobs/international-student-support-and-engagement-officer-launceston-tas-australia": {
      "title": "International Student Support and Engagement Officer",
      "description": "International Student Support and Engagement Officer - Launceston, TAS, Australia Skip to main content Visit UTAS My Profile Kiosk mode Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:26 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:26 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. International Student Support and Engagement Officer 504481 Launceston, TAS Full time Closing on: 22 Nov 2026 Add to favourites View favourites The University of Tasmania acknowledges the palawa/pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present Be the first point of contact for international students at the Australian Maritime College (AMC). Coordinate student engagement, onboarding, and support initiatives that foster belonging and success. Fixed-term contract (2 years), full-time opportunity based at the AMC Newnham Campus, Launceston. About the Opportunity The Australian Maritime College (AMC) is one of the world's leading maritime education and research institutions, attracting students from across the globe to study in Tasmania. As our international student community continues to grow, we're looking for someone who is passionate about supporting students and helping them make the most of their university experience. As the International Student Support and Engagement Officer, you'll be a key point of connection for international students throughout their journey at AMC. You'll provide guidance and support, help students navigate university processes and services, and create opportunities for them to engage with campus life and the broader community. Working closely with colleagues across Student Academic Success, Wellbeing, Advising, and AMC's academic and professional teams, you'll play an important role in fostering a welcoming and inclusive student experience. You'll help students feel connected, supported, and set up for success while contributing to initiatives that strengthen student engagement, retention, and satisfaction. This is a rewarding opportunity for someone who enjoys building relationships, working with people from diverse cultural backgrounds, and making a meaningful difference in students' lives. What you'll do Provide a welcoming first point of contact for international students at AMC. Support student onboarding, orientation, enrolment processes, and administrative activities. Assist students to access academic, wellbeing, advising, and support services across the University. Develop positive relationships with students and help create an inclusive and supportive campus environment. Coordinate and deliver engagement activities that encourage participation, connection, and belonging. Liaise with academic staff, professional teams, and external stakeholders to support student success. Maintain accurate records and contribute to reporting and data collection activities. Support initiatives that improve student satisfaction, retention, and overall experience. Contribute to continuous improvement of student support processes and services while ensuring compliance with University and regulatory requirements. What we're looking for We're looking for someone who enjoys working with people and is genuinely motivated by helping international students succeed. You will bring: Experience providing student support, administration, customer service, or related services in a complex environment. Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to build rapport with people from diverse cultural and linguistic backgrounds. Proven ability to build relationships and collaborate with a broad range of stakeholders. Strong organisational skills and the ability to manage competing priorities while maintaining attention to detail. Sound judgement and the ability to manage sensitive or confidential matters appropriately. Experience coordinating events, programs, or engagement activities. Confidence using enterprise systems and maintaining accurate records. A commitment to delivering high-quality, student-centred services. Experience supporting international students will be highly regarded. Relevant qualifications and/or an equivalent combination of experience and expertise. What’s on Offer? As we look toward 2050, we remain committed to fostering excellence, collaboration and innovation while creating opportunities for our people to make a meaningful impact through teaching and research. You'll be joining a supportive team that is passionate about student success and creating a welcoming experience for students from around the world. You'll have access to an array of staff benefits and discounts including: 26 Weeks paid parental leave for primary caregivers 17% superannuation contribution Health and fitness membership options Accommodation and car hire discounts Health insurance and banking offers Novated leasing Salary Details Appointment to this role will be at HEO 6 and will have a total remuneration package of up to $107,780, comprising a base salary within the range of $92,120 to $99,891 plus 17% superannuation. How to Apply? To apply online, please provide the following supporting documentation: Resume/CV Cover letter outlining your suitability and motivation for the role For current UTAS staff, in submitting your application, you acknowledge you have/intend to discuss your interest in this vacancy with your current manager and understand they may need to be contacted confidentially by the hiring manager as part of the assessment of your application. For further information about this position, please contact Alison Smith, Team Leader, International Student Advice, alison.m.smith@utas.edu.au Please visit https://www.utas.edu.au/jobs/applying for our guide to applying and details on the recruitment process. Please refer to the attached Position Description below for full details. Position Description - International Student Support and Engagement Officer.pdf Applications close Sunday 22nd November 2026, 11.55pm Interviews will be held the week starting 30 November. As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of this role. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 7d36776d Last Name (required) 81486247 Email (required) 963c1977 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Geophysical Data Engineer Hobart, TAS Information Technology, Laboratory & Research Support Develop data systems, workflows and visualisation tools supporting Antarctic Ice Sheet research, analysis and management of complex datasets. Project Lead Hobart, TAS Community & Engagement, Project Management & Support Lead and coordinate a community-led pilot project in New Norfolk, working with children, families, schools and stakeholders to develop and strengthen educational pathways. Senior Lecturer in Medical Education Launceston, TAS Teaching Intensive Curious about academic medicine? Explore a flexible fixed-term teaching opportunity while maintaining your clinical career Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 2da69719 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administration Student Services Administration Student Services Employment Type Full time Full time Locations Launceston, TAS, Australia Launceston, TAS, Australia First Name (required) 1eccaadf Last Name (required) 32831810 Email (required) 9331de6f Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026  University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Cookie Preferences Copyright Statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
