    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/jobs/project-officer-hobart-tas-australia-b9bf2b92-c82b-4917-bd6b-b6d1c5be26fd": {
      "title": "Project Officer",
      "description": "Project Officer - Hobart, TAS, Australia Skip to main content Visit UTAS My Profile Kiosk mode Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:26 Loaded : 0% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:26 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Project Officer 504489 Hobart, TAS Part time Closing on: 22 Nov 2026 The University of Tasmania acknowledges the palawa/pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present Join a growing National research initiative with more than 5000 participants. Coordinate project activities including participant engagement, ethics applications, data management, budgets and community events. Fixed-term for 2 years, part-time (0.5) opportunity based in Hobart. About the Opportunity The Tasmania Parkinson's Project is a collaborative initiative bringing together researchers, clinicians and the Parkinson's community to better understand Parkinson’s and improve the lives of people living with the condition. Since commencing two years ago, the project has experienced significant growth and now supports a cohort of more than 5000 people across Australia. Alongside its research program, the project delivers webinars, community education sessions, links to the UTAS-developed Parkinson’s Massive Open Online Course (MOOC), participant engagement activities and innovative online learning opportunities that help connect people with information, services and support. As the Project Officer, you will play a key role in coordinating project activities and supporting the successful delivery of research and community engagement initiatives. Working closely with researchers, project partners and participants, you will contribute to participant recruitment and retention, ethics administration, data governance, database management, budgets, event coordination and stakeholder engagement. This is an exciting opportunity for a highly organised and proactive professional who enjoys working with people, managing diverse activities and contributing to research that makes a meaningful difference to the Tasmanian community. What you'll do Coordinate day-to-day project activities to support the successful delivery of project objectives and milestones. Support participant recruitment, engagement and retention activities. Prepare, submit and manage human research ethics applications and associated data governance documentation. Maintain project databases, records, financial records and data management processes. Coordinate webinars, participant engagement days and community education activities. Assist with project communications including newsletters, website content and stakeholder updates. Liaise with researchers, clinicians, project partners and community stakeholders. Support project governance activities, meetings and reporting requirements. Provide administrative and secretariat support to advisory groups and committees. Contribute to continuous improvement activities and project growth initiatives. What we're looking for We're looking for a highly organised and collaborative professional who is motivated by supporting research and improving health outcomes for the community. You will bring: Relevant qualifications and/or an equivalent combination of experience and expertise. Demonstrated experience in project coordination, administration or research support. Strong organisational skills with the ability to manage competing priorities and deadlines. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills. Experience maintaining databases, records and information management systems. Proven ability to build productive relationships with a diverse range of stakeholders. Strong attention to detail and the ability to work independently and as part of a team. Experience supporting ethics, governance or compliance processes will be highly regarded. Experience working in health, research, higher education or community-based environments will be advantageous. A commitment to high-quality service and continuous improvement. What’s on Offer? As we look toward 2050, we remain committed to fostering excellence, collaboration and innovation while creating opportunities for our people to make a meaningful impact through teaching and research. You'll be joining a collaborative team delivering research and engagement activities that are making a real difference to the lives of people living with Parkinson's and their families. You'll have access to an array of staff benefits and discounts including: 26 Weeks paid parental leave for primary caregivers 17% superannuation contribution Health and fitness membership options Accommodation and car hire discounts Health insurance and banking offers Novated leasing Salary Details Appointment to this role will be at HEO 6 and will have a total remuneration package of up to $107,780, comprising a base salary within the range of $92,120 to $99,891 plus 17% superannuation. How to Apply? To apply online, please provide the following supporting documentation: Resume/CV Cover letter addressing the selection criteria and outlining your suitability and motivation for the role (Maximum of 2 pages) For current UTAS staff, in submitting your application, you acknowledge you have/intend to discuss your interest in this vacancy with your current manager and understand they may need to be contacted confidentially by the hiring manager as part of the assessment of your application. For further information about this position, please contact Michele Callisaya michele.callisaya@utas.edu.au or Jane Alty jane.alty@utas.edu.au Project Co-Leads Please visit https://www.utas.edu.au/jobs/applying for our guide to applying and details on the recruitment process. Please refer to the attached Position Description below for full details. Position Description - Project Officer Tasmania Parkinsons Project.pdf Applications close Sunday 22nd November 2026, 11.55pm Interviews will be held Monday 7th December 2026 for shortlisted applicants. As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of this role. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) bba4893d Last Name (required) 58fed239 Email (required) a0807ab7 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Geophysical Data Engineer Hobart, TAS Information Technology, Laboratory & Research Support Develop data systems, workflows and visualisation tools supporting Antarctic Ice Sheet research, analysis and management of complex datasets. Project Lead Hobart, TAS Community & Engagement, Project Management & Support Lead and coordinate a community-led pilot project in New Norfolk, working with children, families, schools and stakeholders to develop and strengthen educational pathways. Senior Lecturer in Medical Education Launceston, TAS Teaching Intensive Curious about academic medicine? Explore a flexible fixed-term teaching opportunity while maintaining your clinical career Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 6986cce3 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Project Management & Support Project Management & Support Employment Type Part time Part time Locations Hobart, TAS, Australia Hobart, TAS, Australia First Name (required) 65cd6901 Last Name (required) b6e67048 Email (required) 89d1d8ee Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026  University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Cookie Preferences Copyright Statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
