    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/jobs/team-leader-student-enquiries-hobart-tas-australia-launceston-burnie": {
      "title": "Team Leader, Student Enquiries",
      "description": "Team Leader, Student Enquiries - Hobart, TAS, Australia - Launceston, TAS, Australia - Burnie, TAS, Australia Skip to main content Visit UTAS My Profile Kiosk mode Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:26 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:26 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Team Leader, Student Enquiries 504435 Burnie, TAS Hobart, TAS Launceston, TAS Full time Closing on: 15 Nov 2026 Add to favourites View favourites The University of Tasmania acknowledges the Palawa/Pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. Provide strategic and operational leadership for the University-wide Student Enquiries Service, managing workforce planning, staff development, performance and wellbeing to deliver a consistent, high-quality student experience. Lead the resolution of complex and sensitive student matters, build strong stakeholder partnerships, and drive service improvement initiatives that enhance student recruitment, retention and institutional performance. Full time, Fixed-Term (1 December 2026 - 31 May 2027) position located in either Hobart, Burnie or Launceston. About the opportunity The Team Leader, Student Enquiries provides operational leadership for the University-wide Student Enquiries Service within the UniConnect model, exercising independent judgement to manage complex, time-critical and high-risk matters that impact student outcomes, service delivery and institutional risk. The role is responsible for workforce planning, recruitment, capability development, performance management and staff wellbeing, ensuring a high-performing and student-centred service. As the primary operational authority for Student Enquiries, the Team Leader manages sensitive student issues, ensures compliance with duty of care obligations, mitigates operational and reputational risks, and leads cross-functional stakeholder engagement, service improvement initiatives and conversion activities that support student recruitment, retention and overall institutional performance. What you’ll do: Lead strategic workforce planning and recruitment: Develop and implement staffing strategies that support service continuity, peak period responsiveness, and long-term capability building. Coordinate recruitment campaigns and onboarding processes. Lead people management and staff support initiatives: Oversee complex performance management processes, facilitate behavioural coaching, and support return-to-work and other HR-aligned plans. Foster a cohesive team culture by ensuring staff behaviours align with group expectations and contribute to a unified, high-performing environment. Provide senior first‑response leadership for complex and high‑risk student wellbeing situations, exercising unsupervised judgement in matters involving emotional distress, safety, grief, cultural considerations, visa implications and duty‑of‑care obligations prior to referral to specialist services. Drive service innovation and process improvement: Lead projects that improve enquiry handling, system usability, and student experience. Collaborate with internal stakeholders to pilot new approaches and evaluate impact. Provide strategic reporting and insights: Analyse service data, feedback, and workforce metrics to inform decision-making. Prepare reports and recommendations for leadership and contribute to strategic planning forums. ­ What we’re looking for: Sound understanding of student support frameworks, duty of‑ care obligations and the management of complex or high‑ risk‑ student matters within a university setting. Strong knowledge of university operations, policy environments and regulatory considerations, with the ability to apply judgement where policy or precedent is insufficient. Proficiency in the use of reporting, planning and project management tools to analyse performance, identify risks and inform decision making in time‑ critical‑ environments. Demonstrated experience in leading strategic coordination across complex service environments, including workforce planning, service design and operational delivery in high-volume, demand‑ driven contexts. Demonstrated capability in leading service innovation, continuous improvement and change initiatives within complex operational settings. Salary details Appointment to this role will be at HEO 8 and will have a total remuneration package of up to $152,033 comprising base salary within the range of $114,282 to $129,943 plus 17% superannuation. How to Apply To apply online, please provide your CV and 1-2-page cover letter outlining your interest in the role, skills, capabilities and experience.  You do not need to separately address the success profile. For further information about this position, please contact Grant Cooper, Manager, Student Enquiries, Grant.Cooper@utas.edu.au or 6226 1423 Please visit https://www.utas.edu.au/jobs/applying for our guide to applying and details on the recruitment process. For current UTAS staff, in submitting your application, you acknowledge you have/intend to discuss your interest in this vacancy with your current manager and understand they may need to be contacted confidentially by the hiring manager as part of the assessment of your application. Please refer to the attached Position Description Below for full details. Position Description - Team Leader Student Enquiries.pdf . Applications close Sunday, 15 November 2026, 11.55pm As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of this role. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) c8ec3a85 Last Name (required) 5ba728a2 Email (required) 006aa2e1 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Geophysical Data Engineer Hobart, TAS Information Technology, Laboratory & Research Support Develop data systems, workflows and visualisation tools supporting Antarctic Ice Sheet research, analysis and management of complex datasets. Project Lead Hobart, TAS Community & Engagement, Project Management & Support Lead and coordinate a community-led pilot project in New Norfolk, working with children, families, schools and stakeholders to develop and strengthen educational pathways. Senior Lecturer in Medical Education Launceston, TAS Teaching Intensive Curious about academic medicine? Explore a flexible fixed-term teaching opportunity while maintaining your clinical career Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 0de75c1f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Management Student Services Management Student Services Employment Type Full time Full time Locations Burnie, TAS, Australia Hobart, TAS, Australia Launceston, TAS, Australia Burnie, TAS, Australia Hobart, TAS, Australia Launceston, TAS, Australia First Name (required) 6c6f6fc5 Last Name (required) 2be54e08 Email (required) f838db3c Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026  University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Cookie Preferences Copyright Statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
