    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/jobs/learning-research-librarian-sydney-nsw-australia": {
      "title": "Learning & Research Librarian",
      "description": "Learning & Research Librarian - Sydney, NSW, Australia Skip to main content Visit UTAS My Profile Kiosk mode Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 0:00 Loaded : 0% Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 0:00 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles captions and subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Learning & Research Librarian 504487 Sydney, NSW Part time Closing on: 29 Nov 2026 Create and deliver learning experiences that build research, information and digital literacy skills. Work independently, take initiative, and enjoy building meaningful connections with students, staff and colleagues. Ongoing, Part time (0.6) role based in Rozelle, Sydney. The University of Tasmania acknowledges the Palawa/Pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. About the opportunity The University of Tasmania is looking for a Learning & Research Librarian to provide dedicated support to students and staff as the sole librarian at our Rozelle campus in Sydney. As our new Learning and Research Librarian, you will help create an inclusive and engaging learning environment that empowers students, researchers and staff to succeed. You will design and deliver innovative learning resources and services that build information literacy, support research excellence, and reflect the diverse needs of our university community. Working collaboratively across Library and Cultural Collections, you will build strong partnerships to ensure support is accessible, relevant and available when and where it is needed. In this role, you will work across a broad range of disciplines and scholarship levels, from pre-degree students through to senior researchers. While your focus will typically span the wider University community, opportunities may arise to develop specialist expertise in particular disciplines or areas of learning and research support. Our ideal candidate thrives in a collaborative environment, takes initiative, and enjoys building meaningful connections with students, staff and colleagues. As the dedicated librarian at our Rozelle campus, you will play an important role in creating a visible and supportive local library presence for the services and functions of Library and Cultural Collections. Success in this role requires excellent communication and relationship-building skills, resilience, a commitment to delivering high-quality on-campus support, and the ability to work autonomously while maintaining strong connections with colleagues across the University. What you’ll do: Develop and deliver information literacy programs and resources that align with University strategy and curriculum, building students’ research and critical thinking skills. Support effective use of scholarly information resources across the research lifecycle to enable research excellence. Develop and promote open scholarship initiatives that improve equitable access to information. Provide specialist support to a diverse university community, ensuring services are inclusive and responsive to community needs. Build strong engagement with the university community through information support, consultation and collaboration with schools. ­ What we’re looking for: A relevant degree with several years’ subsequent experience, or an equivalent combination of relevant experience and/or education/training. Knowledge of scholarly resources and publishing practices across disciplines. Ability to create engaging and accessible learning experiences that support student and research success. Understanding of user experience principles and their application to service improvement. Adaptability in using and recommending emerging technologies to support the academic journey. Experience working in an academic library. Salary details Appointment to this role will be at HEO 6 and will have a total remuneration package of up to $116,872 (pro rata) comprising base salary within the range of $92,120 to $99,891 plus 17% superannuation. How to Apply To apply online, please provide your CV and 1-2-page cover letter outlining your interest in the role, skills, capabilities and experience.  You do not need to separately address the success profile. For further information about this position, please contact Chris Evans – Manager, Library Learning and Research at Christine.Evans@utas.edu.au Please visit https://www.utas.edu.au/jobs/applying for our guide to applying and details on the recruitment process. For current UTAS staff, in submitting your application, you acknowledge you have/intend to discuss your interest in this vacancy with your current manager and understand they may need to be contacted confidentially by the hiring manager as part of the assessment of your application. Please refer to the attached Position Description below for full details. Position Description - 504487 - Learning & Research Librarian.pdf Applications close Sunday, 29 November 2026, 11.55pm As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of this role. Back to job search Recommended Jobs Geophysical Data Engineer Hobart, TAS Information Technology, Laboratory & Research Support Develop data systems, workflows and visualisation tools supporting Antarctic Ice Sheet research, analysis and management of complex datasets. Project Lead Hobart, TAS Community & Engagement, Project Management & Support Lead and coordinate a community-led pilot project in New Norfolk, working with children, families, schools and stakeholders to develop and strengthen educational pathways. Senior Lecturer in Medical Education Launceston, TAS Teaching Intensive Curious about academic medicine? Explore a flexible fixed-term teaching opportunity while maintaining your clinical career © 2026  University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Cookie Preferences Copyright Statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
